    <h2 class="avader-title">AGH AVADER Student Research Group</h2>
    <p>
      AVADER is the student research group run by our team at the Department of Automatic Control and Robotics, active since 2014/2015. Its members
      build embedded perception and control systems for mobile robots: drones (UAVs), autonomous cars, driver-assistance systems (ADAS) and advanced
      video surveillance. They process data from vision, thermal and event cameras, radar and LiDAR, using classical algorithms and embedded AI
      (TinyML). Projects run on FPGA and SoC FPGA boards (ZCU104, Kria, Versal), NVIDIA Jetson and Raspberry Pi 5, with ROS, Gazebo and NVIDIA Isaac
      Sim for prototyping and hardware-in-the-loop tests.
    </p>
    <p>
      <strong>What we do:</strong> international competitions (Xilinx Open Hardware, the UAV competition at ICUAS, MathWorks Minidrone Challenge), AGH
      student research conferences, scientific papers, projects funded by AGH Rector's Grants, and science outreach at AGH Open Days and Researchers'
      Night.
    </p>
